AB  - The research is devoted to analyzing the stability of cryptocurrency systems under threats associated with the development of quantum computing. The paper proposes a differential game model to formalize the interaction between cryptocurrency systems and quantum computers (QCs). The methodology uses differential game theory to model the dynamics of the parties' resource allocation and evaluate their player strategies. During the modeling process, scenarios of confrontation between cryptocurrency technologies and quantum computing were analyzed to identify key patterns and factors affecting the effectiveness of cryptographic protection and the computational capabilities of attackers. The results obtained may become the basis for the development of new cryptographic security standards and the formation of adaptive strategies for the protection of digital assets in the context of the growing capabilities of quantum computing and quantum computers. Β© 2025 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
