AB  - The study is devoted to the analysis of the stability of cryptocurrency systems in the face of threats associated with the development of quantum computing. The paper proposes a differential game model that allows formalizing the interaction of cryptographic systems and quantum computers (QC). The methodology is based on the use of differential game theory to model the dynamics of the distribution of resources of the parties and assess their strategies of the players. In the process of modeling, scenarios of confrontation between cryptocurrency technologies and quantum computing were analyzed, which made it possible to identify key patterns and factors affecting the effectiveness of cryptographic protection and the computational capabilities of attackers. The results obtained can form the basis for the development of new standards of cryptographic security and the formation of adaptive strategies for protecting digital assets in the face of growing capabilities of quantum computing and quantum computers. Β© 2025 IEEE.
