AB  - A breakthrough in payment system protection comes from Quantum Homomorphic Fraud Analytics,which merges homomorphic encryption (HE) capabilities with quantum computing algorithms.This framework provides absolute protection because it directly enables the analysis of encryptedpayment data, which meets privacy requirements, GDPR, and other modern data protection laws.Using quantum algorithms, this system speeds up computational operations of classical HE, makingit possible to detect fraud in real-time without losing efficiency or security capabilities. Byimplementing quantum-resistant encryption standards, the system defends financial systems frompresent and future quantum threats. With superlative precision, the system detects sophisticatedfraud patterns, unusual transaction patterns, and behavioral irregularities through quantum machinelearning integration. The system design features high scalability, which allows it to process UPIand blockchain-based remittance transactions alongside low-latency operations. The fraud detectionplatform based on quantum technology provides complete information protection and advanced detectionsystems backed by impenetrable security, which outpaces industry standards for financialsecurity measures. This groundbreaking framework allows financial institutions to gain better operationalefficiency by providing secure quantum-resilient protections for raw data and enhancedtrust, enabling them to lead the development of payment security into the future. Β© 2026 Sriramulu Bojjagani, V. Dinesh Reddy and Sumalatha Saleti CRC Press is an imprint of Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.
