AB  - Healthcare 5.0 empowered the advancement in several technologies, including medical internet of things, diagnostic systems, telemedicine, big data analytics, security, optimization, and blockchain,. These technologies have several requirements that can be tackled by taking the benefits of the quantum technology based on quantum computers which are incredibly effective and fast. Quantum computing (QC) allows the improvement in semiconductor technologies, and fiberoptic-based communication, which support healthcare. In medicine, applying the quantum theory improves the success rate of preclinical decisions for early diagnosis of diseases as well as supports the prognosis, and treatment along with the understanding of the drug interactions. With the long-term progress, quantum computers could be employed in designing new medicines and solve complex problems in healthcare. The healthcare industry can also have new insights, and optimize several processes for delivering efficient and personalized treatment with the outstanding abilities of quantum computers. In addition, QC enables healthcare scientists to conduct various simulations while designing ideal new approaches concurrently. Typically, the power of quantum solutions gives a range of studies to improve diagnosis, treatment, clinical research, and genomics. Thus the impact of QC could develop an extensive variation of healthcare industries by improving the accuracy and the speed of various tasks and applications, as discussed in this chapter. This chapter covered the most cutting-edge applications of QC to modernize medicine with empowering Healthcare 5.0. It outlines the strategic development for exploiting new QC-based techniques for potential healthcare services. Β© 2025 Elsevier Inc. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
