AB  - E-waste,commonly known as e-waste,encompasses discarded electronics and electrical goods that are no longer functional or useful.The increasing utilization of electrical and electronic equipment,coupled with their tendency for early obsolescence,has led to a significant surge in the production of e-waste. In response to the mounting concerns surrounding e-waste disposal,this study proposes the integration of quantum blockchain technology into e-waste management systems.By harnessing principles rooted inquantummechanics,such as superposition and entanglement,this platformensures securerecord-keeping and transactions,therebyfostering trust among users and stakeholders.Furthermore,the incorporation of quantumblockchain enhances the functionality and usability of the system through optimized algorithms for search,access control,and user interface logic.This research underscores how quantum blockchain technology can revolutionize e-waste management, stressing the E-Waste Facility Locator's vital role in advancing sustainable practices for a greener future. Β© 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
