AB  - This chapter highlights the important applications future healthcare sector using QC (quantum computing). Quantum-related computing has the potential to drastically change a variety of sectors, including healthcare, by greatly accelerating the speed and accuracy of processes like drug research, personalized treatment, and medical imaging. An examination of the existing literature on the subject reveals the many uses of QC in the healthcare industry as well as the state of research in this area. To completely understand the ramifications of QC in the healthcare industry, additional study is needed. Healthcare plays a crucial role in human existence. It is essential that quantum artificial intelligence (AI) be used in the medical field. A few case studies have been looked at in this context to offer some healthcare perspective. Here, we'll focus on the evolution of healthcare in light of the Fourth Industrial Revolution. This chapter describes the transition from β€Industry 1.0β€ to β€Industry 4.0β€ and from β€Healthcare 1.0β€ to β€Healthcare 4.0.β€ Better information and more individualised care are only two ways that the Fourth Industrial Revolution may enhance patient care. IOT, AI, Big Data and Block Chain are a few of the technologies that have improved the effectiveness and efficiency of healthcare. Early illness identification and prediction can be aided by predictive data analysis. Blockchain technology can be used to secure sensitive patient data that is gathered by wearable sensors that are linked to the Internet of Things. Medical practitioners have real-time access to and analysis of the data. The applications covered in this chapter will be very beneficial to modern medicine, and Healthcare 4.0 seems to have endless possibilities. Using data from high-income nations, the medical sector's efforts toward health value chain development 4.0 are being assessed. This chapter examines the data on patients' symptoms, diagnosis, and ongoing care. Β© 2025 Elsevier Inc. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
