AB  - The rapid growth of digital banking has made the security of the online banking transactions very important. Cyberthreats such as phishing, man in middle and data breaches pose a serious threat to financial systems and consumer data. Cryptographic techniques are a good solution to these security concerns because they offer secrecy of data, data integrity, authentication as well as non-repudiation. The paper will analyze the various cryptography techniques involved in securing online banking transactions which include public key infrastructure (PKI), digital signatures, hash functions, symmetric and asymmetric encryption. Such practices can help to stop unauthorized access and manipulation of confidential information, such as a history of transactions and passwords, as well as personal identification numbers (PINs). The combination of end-to-end encryption and multi-factor authentication will significantly enhance the level of security and ensure the safety of data storage and communication. Also analyzed in the study are the new developments that can enhance the structure of online banking security systems in the future such as blockchain-based security systems and quantum-resistant cryptography. The study indicates the importance of the current trends in cryptographic methods to counter the evolving cyber-attacks and maintain customer trust in online financial services by looking at the current cryptographic methods and evaluating their effectiveness. Β© 2025 IEEE.
