AB  - There's a new communication era coming, and it's called IoT. With the Internet of Things (IoT), objects may generate, receive, and share data with each other without human intervention in real time. Such a world necessitates a high level of security, privacy, authentication, and attack recovery in order to be implemented effectively. Furthermore, in order to secure IoT environments end-to-end, IoT application architectures must be restructured. IoT security will be the subject of this chapter, which will analyse and solve the issues that arise in this environment. The work offers the application of many IoT domains. The proposed security algorithms for light weight cryptography are being studied for applicability across a variety of IoT domains. It's possible to build a dispersed network of nodes or peers on the blockchain that are all located in various parts of the world and don't know or trust one another. The proposed models are end to end frameworks that can be expanded to other applications or domains as required. Lightweight Internet of Things encryption is proposed as a solution for devices with minimal resources. It is possible to modify, replace, and confuse the text in some encryption blocks. Β© 2025
