AB  - The current traditional methods for managing inventory continue to be hampered by slow responses, separate sources of information, a lack of fully automated processes, and low scalability, especially in multi-level inventory environments where large volumes of products are being inventoried. Using AI for forecasting, along with Blockchain for increasing trust and accountability through a chain of record keeping, are two emerging technologies that have the potential for significantly improving their application individually or together in many applications. The purpose of this research is to identify and describe the primary shortcomings of today's digital inventory management systems and to create an integrated model combining the three emerging technologies of AI, Blockchain and Quantum Computing. The integrated model will use AI to predict demand and detect anomalies in demand; provide trusted automation using smart contracts developed through the use of Blockchain; and apply quantum algorithms for optimizing large multi-echelon inventory decisions. A theoretical comparative study was conducted to determine potential improvements to inventory system decision-making regarding accuracy, responsiveness, and fault tolerance. The comparative study demonstrated through simulated inventory operation comparisons that the proposed AI - Blockchain - Quantum framework resulted in improved forecasting accuracy, reduced decision time for inventory-related decisions, and enhanced trust in automated inventory-related decision-making compared to a traditional Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system and an AI-based system.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
