AB  - The development of Body Area Networks for sustained patient health monitoring demands solutions to address security requirements and large-scale implementation needs for wider market acceptance. The authors develop a novel framework that combines Deep Quantum Neural Networks with blockchain capacity to handle existing technical challenges. The proposed design implements parallel quantum processes into blockchain decentralized ledger technology to establish an efficient and scalable secure BAN environment. The DQNN model which utilizes quantum entanglement executes physiological data through superposition rules to achieve optimal resource management outcomes. An optimization of a consensus process in the blockchain segment fulfils the demands of systems performing based on limited resources present in the BAN environments. The given method has decreased simulator delays by 62 percent and energy wastage by 47 percent and indicates a precision of 98.7 percent during the process of detection of security anomalies that is above the standards stipulated by NIST. It has shown improved quantum and classical attack resistance since the set of performance evaluation metrics that it presents provide better protection than traditional systems Adding on to the BANs with this development is an important advantage that expanded their capabilities of applying healthcare solutions at scale. Β© 2025 IEEE.
