AB  - Quantum computing represents a radical shift for the current digital world, especially regarding cryptocurrencies and cybercrime. Its ability to break traditional cryptographic methods poses a significant risk to the security of data and digital assets, facilitating illegal activities such as fraud and financing of terrorism. At the same time, quantum computing can also be useful for enhancing crime-fighting efforts, including enabling the seizure of cryptocurrencies β€“a challenge that currently poses many difficulties for judicial authorities and law enforcement agencies. This paper analyzes the risks and opportunities that quantum computing presents for contemporary criminal policy, emphasizing the need to develop post-quantum solutions that ensure legal security in the digital environment. Β© 2025 Dykinson Bookstore. All rights reserved.
