AB  - Cybersecurity has become more important in the digital era as protecting private information in ever-growing IT systems takes the stage. The key problems cybersecurity is now facingβ€”that of growing sophisticated cybercrimes like ransomware, phishing, and data breachesβ€”are examined in this paper. Emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence, quantum computers, and blockchain provide opportunities to both improve security and expose fresh vulnerabilities. Apart from addressing advancements in cybersecurity technology such as Zero Trust architecture and multi-factor authentication, this paper explores ethical and data privacy issues. The paper also highlights more recent developments in cybersecurity like mobile security, cloud security, and biometric authentication. This study underlines the need of continuous innovation in cybersecurity approaches and technology in order to fight hazards in the digital era. Β© The Institution of Engineering & Technology 2024.
