AB  - This paper introduces a fully decentralized communication platform that enables secure messaging and file sharing by integrating a quantum random number generator (QRANG) to enhance cryptographic strength against future quantum threats. The proposed system leverages blockchain technology for tamper-resistant recordkeeping, distributed storage through IPFS, and end-to-end encryption using quantum-derived entropy. Unlike conventional decentralized applications that rely on classical pseudo-random number generators, our approach utilizes true quantum randomness to generate encryption keys, significantly increasing unpredictability and resistance to cryptanalytic attacks. The architecture is organized into presentation, orchestration, and data storage layers to ensure clear separation of functions and facilitate robust security. Empirical evaluation demonstrates substantial improvements in randomness quality, key security, and overall system resilience when compared to traditional methods, highlighting the effectiveness of quantum-enhanced cryptography in practical decentralized applications. Β© 2025 IEEE.
