AB  - The main concern of the people these days is to keep their data safe. We are relying on different technologies as far as possible to maintain the integrity of our data in many applications. Blockchain has evolved and been so trusted to keep up our data secure. But if we go around different other technologies, quantum computing comes in a way of blockchain where the blockchain can be attacked with the algorithms of Groverβ€™s and Shorβ€™s. So the blockchain consensus algorithms can be compromised because of the quantum attacks. This paper suggests a solution to this problem by proposing an algorithm named lattice-based proof of work solved by closest vector problem (CVP). As the time complexities of classical computing algorithms and quantum computing algorithms for lattice-based problems are similar, we have chosen CVP. This algorithm can with stand against quantum attacks. Β© 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.
